      ],
      "source": "https://newjersey.wiki/a/Barnegat_Lighthouse",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A severe winter storm in 1920 eroded shoreline up to the base of the lighthouse, prompting the abandonment of the keeper's house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barnegat_Light%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tourism and fishing remain the borough's most prominent industries, echoing its historic reliance on the sea.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barnegat_Light%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Its distinctive red and white coloration makes it a recognizable landmark, and it continues to operate as an active aid to navigation under the U.S. Coast Guard.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://newjersey.wiki/a/Barnegat_Lighthouse",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Originally constructed in 1859, the lighthouse has witnessed over a century and a half of maritime history, enduring storms, shipwrecks, and the evolution of coastal navigation.",
